#: .\templates\base.html:131
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"La nota {name} se encuentra en la <strong>{position}</strong> en clave de "
"Sol. "
msgstr ""
"The note {name} is found on the <strong>{position}</strong> in treble clef. "

#: .\templates\base.html:132
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<br><br>El sostenido eleva la altura un semitono respecto de {name} natural."
msgstr ""
"<br><br>The sharp raises the pitch a semitone relative to natural {name}."

#: .\templates\base.html:133
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<br><br>El bemol reduce la altura un semitono respecto de {name} natural."
msgstr ""
"<br><br>The flat lowers the pitch a semitone relative to natural {name}."

#: .\templates\base.html:134
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<br><br>El doble sostenido eleva la altura dos semitonos (un tono entero) "
"respecto de {name} natural."
msgstr ""
"<br><br>The double sharp raises the pitch two semitones (a whole tone) "
"relative to natural {name}."

#: .\templates\base.html:135
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"<br><br>El doble bemol reduce la altura dos semitonos (un tono entero) "
"respecto de {name} natural."
msgstr ""
"<br><br>The double flat lowers the pitch two semitones (a whole tone) "
"relative to natural {name}."

#: .\templates\base.html:136
msgid "<br><br>Al ser una nota natural, no tiene alteraciones."
msgstr "<br><br>Being a natural note, it has no accidentals."

#: .\templates\base.html:137
msgid ""
"💡 <strong>Observación Teórica:</strong> Cada línea y espacio del pentagrama "
"representa una nota natural consecutiva. Las alteraciones (♯, ♭) se colocan "
"a la izquierda de la nota para modificar su altura sin cambiar su posición "
"gráfica en el pentagrama."
msgstr ""
"💡 <strong>Theory Note:</strong> Each line and space of the staff represents "
"a consecutive natural note. Accidentals (♯, ♭) are placed to the left of the "
"note to modify its pitch without changing its graphic position on the staff."

#: .\templates\base.html:140
msgid "Distancia diatónica:"
msgstr "Diatonic distance:"

#: .\templates\base.html:141
msgid "Semitonos exactos:"
msgstr "Exact semitones:"

#: .\templates\base.html:142
msgid "Es un intervalo mayor estándar, originado de la escala mayor natural."
msgstr ""
"It's a standard major interval, originating from the natural major scale."

#: .\templates\base.html:143
msgid ""
"Es un intervalo justo (perfecto), muy consonante y fundamental en la armonía."
msgstr "It's a perfect interval, very consonant and fundamental in harmony."

#: .\templates\base.html:144
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Una {intervalo} Menor se obtiene reduciendo un semitono respecto de una "
"Mayor."
msgstr "A minor {intervalo} is obtained by lowering a major one by a semitone."

#: .\templates\base.html:145
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Se obtiene elevando un semitono respecto de una {ref}."
msgstr "It's obtained by raising a {ref} interval by a semitone."

#: .\templates\base.html:146
#, python-brace-format
msgid "Se obtiene reduciendo un semitono respecto de una {ref}."
msgstr "It's obtained by lowering a {ref} interval by a semitone."

#: .\templates\base.html:150
msgid ""
"También es conocida como <strong>Tritono</strong>, dividiendo la octava "
"exactamente a la mitad."
msgstr ""
"It's also known as the <strong>Tritone</strong>, dividing the octave exactly "
"in half."

#: .\templates\base.html:151
msgid ""
"Suena muy estable y abierto, como el comienzo del tema de Star Wars o "
"Twinkle Twinkle."
msgstr ""
"Sounds very stable and open, like the start of the Star Wars theme or "
"Twinkle Twinkle."

#: .\templates\base.html:152
msgid ""
"Suena estable pero con una ligera tensión que pide resolver, típico del "
"himno de bodas."
msgstr ""
"Sounds stable but with a slight tension that asks to be resolved, typical of "
"the wedding march."

#: .\templates\base.html:153
msgid "Tiene un carácter triste o melancólico."
msgstr "Has a sad or melancholic character."

#: .\templates\base.html:154
msgid "Tiene un carácter brillante y alegre."
msgstr "Has a bright and cheerful character."

#: .\templates\base.html:155
msgid "Es sumamente tenso y disonante, como la melodía de Tiburón."
msgstr "It's extremely tense and dissonant, like the Jaws theme."

#: .\templates\base.html:156
msgid "Suena muy melódico y romántico (ej. My Bonnie Lies Over the Ocean)."
msgstr "Sounds very melodic and romantic (e.g. My Bonnie Lies Over the Ocean)."

#: .\templates\base.html:157
msgid ""
"Suena inestable, oscuro y disonante, propio del tritono (Los Simpson intro)."
msgstr ""
"Sounds unstable, dark and dissonant, typical of the tritone (The Simpsons "
"intro)."

#: .\templates\base.html:158
msgid "Ambas notas suenan como la misma pero a diferente altura (octava)."
msgstr "Both notes sound like the same one but at a different pitch (octave)."

#: .\templates\base.html:159
msgid "🎧 <em>Consejo Auditivo:</em>"
msgstr "🎧 <em>Ear Training Tip:</em>"

#: .\templates\base.html:160
msgid ""
"💡 <strong>Observación Teórica:</strong> Los intervalos se definen por dos "
"componentes: su número (distancia diatónica contando el nombre de las notas) "
"y su calidad (ajuste fino en semitonos alterando esas notas)."
msgstr ""
"💡 <strong>Theory Note:</strong> Intervals are defined by two components: "
"their number (diatonic distance counting note names) and their quality (fine "
"adjustment in semitones altering those notes)."

#: .\templates\base.html:163
msgid "La segunda y tercera nota fueron intercambiadas."
msgstr "The second and third notes were swapped."

#: .\templates\base.html:164
msgid "La primera y tercera nota fueron intercambiadas."
msgstr "The first and third notes were swapped."

#: .\templates\base.html:165
msgid "Acertaste las dos primeras notas, pero fallaste en la última."
msgstr "You got the first two notes right, but missed the last one."

#: .\templates\base.html:166
msgid ""
"La primera nota fue correcta, pero la dirección o el salto de la melodía "
"posterior fue diferente."
msgstr ""
"The first note was correct, but the direction or leap of the melody "
"afterward was different."

#: .\templates\base.html:167
msgid ""
"La melodía completa tenía una forma o contorno diferente al que elegiste."
msgstr ""
"The whole melody had a different shape or contour than the one you chose."

#: .\templates\base.html:168
msgid "Análisis del error:"
msgstr "Error analysis:"

#: .\templates\base.html:169
msgid ""
"💡 <strong>Consejo:</strong> Presta atención a la forma de la melodía (si "
"sube, si baja, o si repite la nota) antes de intentar identificar las notas "
"exactas. Puedes guiarte dibujando la curva en el aire con tu mano mientras "
"escuchas."
msgstr ""
"💡 <strong>Tip:</strong> Pay attention to the shape of the melody (whether "
"it goes up, down, or repeats the note) before trying to identify the exact "
"notes. You can guide yourself by drawing the curve in the air with your hand "
"while listening."

